        "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-civilian-corps-act-2011#sec-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-civilian-corps-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-civilian-corps-act-2011.pdf, p.6",
      "values:originalText": "In this Act:\nAustralian Civilian Corps Code of Conduct means the Australian\nCivilian Corps Code of Conduct prescribed under subsection 15(1).\nAustralian Civilian Corps employee means a person engaged\nunder section 19.\nAustralian Civilian Corps Values means the Australian Civilian\nCorps Values prescribed under section 12.\nenterprise agreement has the same meaning as in the Fair Work\nAct 2009.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2014C00531\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\n\nSection 6\n\nAustralian Civilian Corps Act 2011\n\nfair work instrument has the same meaning as in the Fair Work\nAct 2009.\noverseas means outside Australia and the Territories.\nPresiding Officer means:\n\n(a) the President of the Senate; or\n\n(b) the Speaker of the House of Representatives.\nSecretary means the Secretary of the Department.\nWR Act collective transitional instrument means an award, a\ncollective agreement or a pre-reform certified agreement (within\nthe meaning of those terms in the Fair Work (Transitional\nProvisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 2009).",
      "skos:definition": "In this Act:\nAustralian Civilian Corps Code of Conduct means the Australian\nCivilian Corps Code of Conduct prescribed under subsection 15(1).\nAustralian Civilian Corps employee means a person engaged\nunder section 19.\nAustralian Civilian Corps Values means the Australian Civilian\nCorps Values prescribed under section 12.\nenterprise agreement has the same meaning as in the Fair Work\nAct 2009.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2014C00531\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\n\nSection 6\n\nAustralian Civilian Corps Act 2011\n\nfair work instrument has the same meaning as in the Fair Work\nAct 2009.\noverseas means outside Australia and the Territories.\nPresiding Officer means:\n\n(a) the President of the Senate; or\n\n(b) the Speaker of the House of Representatives.\nSecretary means the Secretary of the Department.\nWR Act collective transitional instrument means an award, a\ncollective agreement or a pre-reform certified agreement (within\nthe meaning of those terms in the Fair Work (Transitional\nProvisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 2009).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-5-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-5-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6d43b1d659122ef8e07c3d8e68462f39d8e9d2a7ca547bbbcd4ccfb686c46bdb",
      "skos:note": "Definitions of terms used in the Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-civilian-corps-act-2011#sec-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 6,
      "values:originalText": "In this Act:\nAustralian Civilian Corps Code of Conduct means the Australian\nCivilian Corps Code of Conduct prescribed under subsection 15(1).\nAustralian Civilian Corps employee means a person engaged\nunder section 19.\nAustralian Civilian Corps Values means the Australian Civilian\nCorps Values prescribed under section 12.\nenterprise agreement has the same meaning as in the Fair Work\nAct 2009.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2014C00531\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\n\nSection 6\n\nAustralian Civilian Corps Act 2011\n\nfair work instrument has the same meaning as in the Fair Work\nAct 2009.\noverseas means outside Australia and the Territories.\nPresiding Officer means:\n\n(a) the President of the Senate; or\n\n(b) the Speaker of the House of Representatives.\nSecretary means the Secretary of the Department.\nWR Act collective transitional instrument means an award, a\ncollective agreement or a pre-reform certified agreement (within\nthe meaning of those terms in the Fair Work (Transitional\nProvisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 2009)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-5-norm",
