    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-17",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "17 Breaches of the Australian Civilian Corps Code of Conduct",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-civilian-corps-act-2011#sec-17"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-civilian-corps-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-civilian-corps-act-2011.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "Breaches\n\n(1) The Secretary may impose the following sanctions on an\nAustralian Civilian Corps employee who is found (under\nprocedures established under subsection (3)) to have breached the\nAustralian Civilian Corps Code of Conduct:\n\n(a) termination of employment;\n\n(b) re-assignment of duties;\n\n(c) deductions from salary, by way of fine;\n\n(d) a reprimand.\n\n(2) The regulations may prescribe limitations on the power of the\nSecretary to impose sanctions under subsection (1).\nProcedures\n\n(3) The Secretary must establish procedures for determining whether\nan Australian Civilian Corps employee has breached the Australian\nCivilian Corps Code of Conduct.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2014C00531",
      "skos:definition": "Breaches\n\n(1) The Secretary may impose the following sanctions on an\nAustralian Civilian Corps employee who is found (under\nprocedures established under subsection (3)) to have breached the\nAustralian Civilian Corps Code of Conduct:\n\n(a) termination of employment;\n\n(b) re-assignment of duties;\n\n(c) deductions from salary, by way of fine;\n\n(d) a reprimand.\n\n(2) The regulations may prescribe limitations on the power of the\nSecretary to impose sanctions under subsection (1).\nProcedures\n\n(3) The Secretary must establish procedures for determining whether\nan Australian Civilian Corps employee has breached the Australian\nCivilian Corps Code of Conduct.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2014C00531",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-17-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-17-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-17-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "05c239c39f0fed5986e6e0c085651451353feab91453d08a936ddbdbb676f099"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-civilian-corps-act-2011#sec-17",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "17 Breaches of the Australian Civilian Corps Code of Conduct",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 9,
      "values:originalText": "Breaches\n\n(1) The Secretary may impose the following sanctions on an\nAustralian Civilian Corps employee who is found (under\nprocedures established under subsection (3)) to have breached the\nAustralian Civilian Corps Code of Conduct:\n\n(a) termination of employment;\n\n(b) re-assignment of duties;\n\n(c) deductions from salary, by way of fine;\n\n(d) a reprimand.\n\n(2) The regulations may prescribe limitations on the power of the\nSecretary to impose sanctions under subsection (1).\nProcedures\n\n(3) The Secretary must establish procedures for determining whether\nan Australian Civilian Corps employee has breached the Australian\nCivilian Corps Code of Conduct.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2014C00531"
    },
