        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-civilian-corps-act-2011#sec-19"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-civilian-corps-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-civilian-corps-act-2011.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary, on behalf of the Commonwealth, may engage\npersons as employees for the purposes of:\n\n(a) performing, or potentially performing, duties overseas; or\n\n(b) performing duties in Australia that are incidental, preparatory\nor ancillary to the performance, or potential performance, of\nduties overseas;\nor both.\n\n(2) The engagement of an Australian Civilian Corps employee must be\nfor a specified term.\n\n(3) The specified term may be extended, subject to any limitations\nprescribed by the regulations.\n\n(4) The engagement of an Australian Civilian Corps employee may be\nmade subject to conditions notified to the employee, including\nconditions dealing with any of the following matters:\n\n(a) probation;\n\n(b) citizenship;\n\n(c) formal qualifications;\n\n(d) security and character clearances;\n\n(e) health clearances.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2014C00531",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary, on behalf of the Commonwealth, may engage\npersons as employees for the purposes of:\n\n(a) performing, or potentially performing, duties overseas; or\n\n(b) performing duties in Australia that are incidental, preparatory\nor ancillary to the performance, or potential performance, of\nduties overseas;\nor both.\n\n(2) The engagement of an Australian Civilian Corps employee must be\nfor a specified term.\n\n(3) The specified term may be extended, subject to any limitations\nprescribed by the regulations.\n\n(4) The engagement of an Australian Civilian Corps employee may be\nmade subject to conditions notified to the employee, including\nconditions dealing with any of the following matters:\n\n(a) probation;\n\n(b) citizenship;\n\n(c) formal qualifications;\n\n(d) security and character clearances;\n\n(e) health clearances.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2014C00531",
