    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-27",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "27 Prime Minister may issue directions about leave etc. to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-civilian-corps-act-2011#sec-27"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-civilian-corps-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-civilian-corps-act-2011.pdf, p.17",
      "values:originalText": "Commonwealth employers\nCommonwealth employer\n\n(1) For the purposes of this section, each of the following persons is a\nCommonwealth employer:\n\n(a) a person who, on behalf of the Commonwealth, has the\npowers of an employer in respect of an employee of the\nCommonwealth;\n\n(b) a body corporate that:\n\n(i) is established by or under a law of the Commonwealth\nfor a public purpose; and\n\n(ii) has employees;\n\n(c) a company that:\n\n(i) is a wholly-owned Commonwealth company (within the\nmeaning of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013); and\n\n(ii) has employees.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2014C00531",
      "skos:definition": "Commonwealth employers\nCommonwealth employer\n\n(1) For the purposes of this section, each of the following persons is a\nCommonwealth employer:\n\n(a) a person who, on behalf of the Commonwealth, has the\npowers of an employer in respect of an employee of the\nCommonwealth;\n\n(b) a body corporate that:\n\n(i) is established by or under a law of the Commonwealth\nfor a public purpose; and\n\n(ii) has employees;\n\n(c) a company that:\n\n(i) is a wholly-owned Commonwealth company (within the\nmeaning of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013); and\n\n(ii) has employees.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2014C00531",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-27-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-27-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-27-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-27-logic-ltl-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c5fc428d31a529be568131c440c6c289a437fd7a523449e2c09f1f691e56e65c",
      "skos:note": "Prime Minister may issue directions about leave etc."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-civilian-corps-act-2011#sec-27",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "27 Prime Minister may issue directions about leave etc. to",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 17,
      "values:originalText": "Commonwealth employers\nCommonwealth employer\n\n(1) For the purposes of this section, each of the following persons is a\nCommonwealth employer:\n\n(a) a person who, on behalf of the Commonwealth, has the\npowers of an employer in respect of an employee of the\nCommonwealth;\n\n(b) a body corporate that:\n\n(i) is established by or under a law of the Commonwealth\nfor a public purpose; and\n\n(ii) has employees;\n\n(c) a company that:\n\n(i) is a wholly-owned Commonwealth company (within the\nmeaning of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013); and\n\n(ii) has employees.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2014C00531"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-27-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-27"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-27-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Issue directions",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-27-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "has powers of an employer in respect of an employee of the Commonwealth",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal relation between powers and employees",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) a person who, on behalf of the Commonwealth, has the powers of an employer in respect of an employee of the Commonwealth;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-27-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "has employees",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Recurring relation between company and employees",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) a body corporate that: (i) is established by or under a law of the Commonwealth for a public purpose; and (ii) has employees;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-28",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "28 Payments in special circumstances",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-civilian-corps-act-2011#sec-28"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-civilian-corps-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-civilian-corps-act-2011.pdf, p.19",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may authorise the making of payments to a person\nunder subsection (2) if the Minister considers it appropriate to do\nso because of special circumstances that relate to, or arise out of:\n\n(a) the payee’s employment as an Australian Civilian Corps\nemployee; or\n\n(b) another person’s employment as an Australian Civilian Corps\nemployee.\n\n(2) The Minister may authorise the making of any of the following\npayments:\n\n(a) one or more payments of an amount or amounts specified in\nthe authorisation (or worked out in accordance with the\nauthorisation);\n\n(b) periodical payments of an amount specified in the\nauthorisation (or worked out in accordance with the\nauthorisation), during a period specified in the authorisation\n(or worked out in accordance with the authorisation).\n\n(3) Payments may be authorised under this section even though the\npayments would not otherwise be authorised by law or required to\nmeet a legal liability.\n\n(4) An authorisation cannot be made under this section if it would\ninvolve, or be likely to involve, a total amount of more than\n$100,000.\n\n(5) Conditions may be attached to payments under this section. If a\ncondition is breached, the payment may be recovered by the\nCommonwealth as a debt in a court of competent jurisdiction.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may authorise the making of payments to a person\nunder subsection (2) if the Minister considers it appropriate to do\nso because of special circumstances that relate to, or arise out of:\n\n(a) the payee’s employment as an Australian Civilian Corps\nemployee; or\n\n(b) another person’s employment as an Australian Civilian Corps\nemployee.\n\n(2) The Minister may authorise the making of any of the following\npayments:\n\n(a) one or more payments of an amount or amounts specified in\nthe authorisation (or worked out in accordance with the\nauthorisation);\n\n(b) periodical payments of an amount specified in the\nauthorisation (or worked out in accordance with the\nauthorisation), during a period specified in the authorisation\n(or worked out in accordance with the authorisation).\n\n(3) Payments may be authorised under this section even though the\npayments would not otherwise be authorised by law or required to\nmeet a legal liability.\n\n(4) An authorisation cannot be made under this section if it would\ninvolve, or be likely to involve, a total amount of more than\n$100,000.\n\n(5) Conditions may be attached to payments under this section. If a\ncondition is breached, the payment may be recovered by the\nCommonwealth as a debt in a court of competent jurisdiction.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-28-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-28-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-28-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-28-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-28-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5e12a76e2eaf42b80964a21782b527863824c1075df02095503a600a23ccf7c5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-civilian-corps-act-2011#sec-28",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "28 Payments in special circumstances",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 19,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may authorise the making of payments to a person\nunder subsection (2) if the Minister considers it appropriate to do\nso because of special circumstances that relate to, or arise out of:\n\n(a) the payee’s employment as an Australian Civilian Corps\nemployee; or\n\n(b) another person’s employment as an Australian Civilian Corps\nemployee.\n\n(2) The Minister may authorise the making of any of the following\npayments:\n\n(a) one or more payments of an amount or amounts specified in\nthe authorisation (or worked out in accordance with the\nauthorisation);\n\n(b) periodical payments of an amount specified in the\nauthorisation (or worked out in accordance with the\nauthorisation), during a period specified in the authorisation\n(or worked out in accordance with the authorisation).\n\n(3) Payments may be authorised under this section even though the\npayments would not otherwise be authorised by law or required to\nmeet a legal liability.\n\n(4) An authorisation cannot be made under this section if it would\ninvolve, or be likely to involve, a total amount of more than\n$100,000.\n\n(5) Conditions may be attached to payments under this section. If a\ncondition is breached, the payment may be recovered by the\nCommonwealth as a debt in a court of competent jurisdiction."
    },
