    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-30",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "30 Delegations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-civilian-corps-act-2011#sec-30"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-civilian-corps-act-2011.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-civilian-corps-act-2011.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, in writing, delegate to:\n\n(a) another Minister; or\n\n(b) an SES employee, or acting SES employee, in the\nDepartment; or\n\n(c) a person who holds an office or appointment under an Act;\nany or all of his or her powers or functions under this Act or the\nregulations.\nNote:\nThe expressions SES employee and acting SES employee are defined\nin the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\n(2) The Secretary may, in writing, delegate to:\n\n(a) an APS employee in the Department; or\n\n(b) an Australian Civilian Corps employee;\nany or all of his or her powers or functions under:\n\n(c) this Act; or\n\n(d) the regulations; or\n\n(e) any other instrument made under this Act.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2014C00531\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 5\n\nSection 31\n\nAustralian Civilian Corps Act 2011\n\nNote:\nThe expression APS employee is defined in the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901.\n\n(3) A person exercising powers or functions under a delegation under\nthis section must comply with any directions of the person who\ndelegated the power or function.\n\n(4) This section does not apply to a power to make, vary or revoke a\nlegislative instrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, in writing, delegate to:\n\n(a) another Minister; or\n\n(b) an SES employee, or acting SES employee, in the\nDepartment; or\n\n(c) a person who holds an office or appointment under an Act;\nany or all of his or her powers or functions under this Act or the\nregulations.\nNote:\nThe expressions SES employee and acting SES employee are defined\nin the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\n(2) The Secretary may, in writing, delegate to:\n\n(a) an APS employee in the Department; or\n\n(b) an Australian Civilian Corps employee;\nany or all of his or her powers or functions under:\n\n(c) this Act; or\n\n(d) the regulations; or\n\n(e) any other instrument made under this Act.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2014C00531\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 5\n\nSection 31\n\nAustralian Civilian Corps Act 2011\n\nNote:\nThe expression APS employee is defined in the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901.\n\n(3) A person exercising powers or functions under a delegation under\nthis section must comply with any directions of the person who\ndelegated the power or function.\n\n(4) This section does not apply to a power to make, vary or revoke a\nlegislative instrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-30-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-30-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-30-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-civilian-corps-act-2011-sec-30-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2d74a49614124716887c6c366ede37cc56fdfcdaff2b803ad7ae1a49bdd1fa19"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-civilian-corps-act-2011#sec-30",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "30 Delegations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, in writing, delegate to:\n\n(a) another Minister; or\n\n(b) an SES employee, or acting SES employee, in the\nDepartment; or\n\n(c) a person who holds an office or appointment under an Act;\nany or all of his or her powers or functions under this Act or the\nregulations.\nNote:\nThe expressions SES employee and acting SES employee are defined\nin the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\n(2) The Secretary may, in writing, delegate to:\n\n(a) an APS employee in the Department; or\n\n(b) an Australian Civilian Corps employee;\nany or all of his or her powers or functions under:\n\n(c) this Act; or\n\n(d) the regulations; or\n\n(e) any other instrument made under this Act.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2014C00531\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 5\n\nSection 31\n\nAustralian Civilian Corps Act 2011\n\nNote:\nThe expression APS employee is defined in the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901.\n\n(3) A person exercising powers or functions under a delegation under\nthis section must comply with any directions of the person who\ndelegated the power or function.\n\n(4) This section does not apply to a power to make, vary or revoke a\nlegislative instrument."
    },
